# Wireframe: Revert Toast

## Purpose & Flow Context

The Revert Toast appears when an optimistic update fails — the user changed an issue's status, assigned an issue, or updated a project, the UI reflected the change immediately, but the API call failed and the state reverted. The toast informs the user of the failure and offers retry. Entry: optimistic update failure (API error or network loss). Exit: user dismisses toast, retries, or toast auto-dismisses after 5 seconds.

---

## Notation Legend

| Symbol | Meaning | Symbol | Meaning |
|--------|---------|--------|---------|
| `[...]` | Button / interactive element | `[>...▼]` | Dropdown |
| `_______` | Text input / editable field | `[X]` | Close / dismiss |
| `⚠` | Warning / due date | `📎N` | N attachments |
| `💬N` | N comments | `🔗` | Card relationship |
| `👤` | User / mention | `○ ●` | Radio unselected / selected |

## Accessibility — Shared Conventions

All interactive screens inherit these. Per-screen specifics noted where they diverge.

| Concern | Convention |
|---------|------------|
| Landmarks | `header`, `main`, `aside`, `contentinfo` |
| Heading order | One `h1` per screen, `h2` for sections |
| Accessible names | Icon-only controls get `aria-label` |
| Keyboard | Tab, Enter/Space, Escape, Arrow keys |
| Target size | ≥24×24 CSS px reservation |
| Non-color intent | Icon + text, never color alone |

---

## Layout Regions

**Grid**: Toast is positioned fixed, not part of grid layout.

**App-shell**: Toast overlays content, positioned bottom-right (same placement as ReconnectionToast).

| Region | Content | Notes |
|--------|---------|-------|
| Toast Container | Error icon, message text, retry button, dismiss button | Fixed position, bottom-right, z-index high |

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                                                                    |
|                                                                    |
|                                                                    |
|                                                                    |
|                                                                    |
|  +------------------------------------------------------------+  |
|  |  ✗  Status update failed.  [Retry]  [X]                   |  |
|  +------------------------------------------------------------+  |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

*Legend: [{Button}] [Input] [Link] [#Heading] [>Dropdown] [Avatar] [Icon]*

## Components & Affordances

| Element | DS Component | Behavior | Edge Cases |
|---------|-------------|----------|------------|
| Error Icon | Icon | Visual indicator of failure state | None |
| Message Text | Text | Describes what failed | Truncates if too long; varies by action type |
| Retry Button | Button | Click re-initiates the failed action | Disabled during retry attempt |
| Dismiss Button | Button | Click closes toast | Keyboard accessible via Escape |

## Data Display

This is a notification toast, not a data display screen. It communicates optimistic update failure and offers recovery.

## Content & Microcopy Intent

| Slot | Intent | Notes |
|------|--------|-------|
| Error Icon | Visual failure indicator | ✗ circle icon (distinct from ⚠ warning on ReconnectionToast) |
| Message Text | Communicates what failed and why | "{Action} failed. Your change has been reverted.", "Unable to save. Check your connection." |
| Retry Button | Offers action recovery | "Retry", "Try again" |
| Dismiss Button | Allows user to dismiss | [X] icon |

### Message Variants by Action Type

| Action | Message |
|--------|---------|
| Issue status change | "Status update failed. Your change has been reverted." |
| Issue assignment | "Assignment failed. Issue returned to previous assignee." |
| Project update | "Project save failed. Your changes have been reverted." |
| Network failure | "Network error. Your change could not be saved." |

## States

### Visible (Optimistic Update Failed)

Toast appears with error icon, failure message, and retry button.

```
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|  ✗  Status update failed.  [Retry]  [X]                   |
+------------------------------------------------------------+
```

### Visible (Network Failure)

Toast appears with network-specific message.

```
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|  ✗  Network error. Your change could not be saved.  [Retry]  [X] |
+------------------------------------------------------------+
```

### Loading (Retry in Progress)

Retry button shows loading spinner, disabled.

```
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|  ✗  Retrying...  [⟳ Retry]  [X]                            |
+------------------------------------------------------------+
```

### Dismissed

Toast slides out to right and is removed from DOM.

```
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|  (empty - toast has slid out)                               |
+------------------------------------------------------------+
```

## Responsive

| Breakpoint | Changes |
|------------|---------|
| Desktop (>1024px) | Full toast with all elements, bottom-right position |
| Tablet (768-1024px) | Same as desktop |
| Mobile (<768px) | Toast spans full width at bottom, larger touch targets |

## Accessibility — Screen Composition

| Concern | Implementation |
|---------|----------------|
| Landmarks | No landmarks (toast is overlay) |
| Heading order | No headings in toast |
| Reading / Focus order | Focus moves to toast when it appears |
| Accessible names | Retry button: aria-label="Retry {action}", Dismiss button: aria-label="Dismiss notification" |
| Keyboard operability | Tab to buttons, Enter/Space activates, Escape dismisses toast |
| Target size | ≥24×24 CSS px on Retry and Dismiss buttons |
| Focus not obscured | Toast doesn't obscure focused element (positioned bottom-right) |
| Non-color intent | Error icon + text, not just red color |

## Assumptions

- **Component reuse**: RevertToast follows the same visual pattern as ReconnectionToast (fixed-position toast, bottom-right) but is a separate component with distinct semantics: ReconnectionToast handles WebSocket connection failures; RevertToast handles optimistic update failures. Both share the toast anatomy but are triggered by different flows and display different message variants.
- **DS entry**: RevertToast is added to the design-system catalog as a distinct component (see design-system.md).
- **Single toast at a time**: Only one toast (RevertToast or ReconnectionToast) is visible at a time. If both triggers fire simultaneously, the most recent toast takes precedence.
